{"name":"Jungle Beat","hex":"#654f2d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"jungle","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large, lush, undeveloped, humid forest, especially in a tropical region, thick with vegetation and wildlife; a tropical  rainforest.","Any uncultivated tract of forest or scrub habitat."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["(Of musical beat, rhythm, etc.) resembling the fast-paced drumming of traditional peoples of the jungle."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jungle"},{"term":"beat","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A stroke; a blow.","A pulsation or throb."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To hit; to strike.","To strike or pound repeatedly, usually in some sort of rhythm."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beat"}],"entries":[{"title":"Donkey Kong Jungle Beat","blocks":[{"text":"Donkey Kong Jungle Beat is a 2004 platform game developed and published by Nintendo for the GameCube. It follows the gorilla Donkey Kong as he sets out to defeat a series of evil kings to conquer the jungle. Jungle Beat is designed for use with the DK Bongos, a bongo drum-style GameCube controller created for the Donkey Konga (2003) rhythm game. The player controls Donkey Kong through various side-scrolling levels as he collects bananas, swings on vines, chains combos, rides animals, and defeats enemies and bosses."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/8e/Donkey_Kong_Jungle_Beat_Coverart.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Donkey_Kong_Jungle_Beat","wikidata":"Q936413"},{"title":"Jungle music","blocks":[{"text":"Jungle is a genre of electronic music that developed in the 1990s out of the UK rave scene and Jamaican sound system culture. Emerging from breakbeat hardcore, the style is characterised by rapid breakbeats, heavily syncopated percussive loops, samples and synthesised effects, combined with the deep basslines, melodies and vocal samples found in dub, reggae and dancehall, as well as hip-hop and funk. Many producers frequently sampled the \"Amen break\" or other breakbeats from funk and jazz recordings. Jungle was a direct precursor to the drum and bass genre which emerged in the mid-1990s."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jungle_music","wikidata":"Q1102161"},{"title":"Jungle Beat (TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Jungle Beat is a family-friendly South African series of animated, self-contained, dialogue-free, five-minute episodes focusing on different animals and the bizarre situations they encounter in nature."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jungle_Beat_(TV_series)","wikidata":"Q31090460"},{"title":"Jungle","blocks":[{"text":"A jungle is an area of land covered with dense forest and tangled vegetation, usually in tropical climates. Application of the term has varied greatly during the past century. Because jungles occur on all inhabited landmasses and may incorporate numerous vegetation and land types in different climatic zones, the wildlife of jungles cannot be straightforwardly defined."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/%E1%9E%96%E1%9F%92%E1%9E%9A%E1%9F%83%E1%9E%80%E1%9E%98%E1%9F%92%E1%9E%96%E1%9E%BB%E1%9E%87%E1%9E%B6.jpg/330px-%E1%9E%96%E1%9F%92%E1%9E%9A%E1%9F%83%E1%9E%80%E1%9E%98%E1%9F%92%E1%9E%96%E1%9E%BB%E1%9E%87%E1%9E%B6.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jungle","wikidata":"Q191086"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/5/52/DKJB_Screenshot.png/330px-DKJB_Screenshot.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/5/52/DKJB_Screenshot.png/330px-DKJB_Screenshot.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A screenshot of the first level. The combo count builds up based on how many objects Donkey Kong bounces off of without touching the ground.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADKJB_Screenshot.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Yoshiaki_Koizumi_2007.jpg/500px-Yoshiaki_Koizumi_2007.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Yoshiaki_Koizumi_2007.jpg/500px-Yoshiaki_Koizumi_2007.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AYoshiaki_Koizumi_2007.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/DK-Bongos.JPG/500px-DK-Bongos.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/DK-Bongos.JPG/1280px-DK-Bongos.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/DK-Bongos.JPG/500px-DK-Bongos.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADK-Bongos.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Nintendo-GameCube-Console-FL.jpg/500px-Nintendo-GameCube-Console-FL.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Nintendo-GameCube-Console-FL.jpg/1280px-Nintendo-GameCube-Console-FL.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Nintendo-GameCube-Console-FL.jpg/500px-Nintendo-GameCube-Console-FL.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Donkey Kong Jungle Beat was released for the GameCube (pictured) in Japan in December 2004 and in the West in early 2005.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANi